# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# spec-spine: only the wall-clock build metadata is derived-and-ignored
.derived/**/build-meta.json
.derived/attestation/
# claude-observatory state root for this project
data/
# local overlays
.idea/
.DS_Store

# subagent scratch memory written by the reviewer agent; never corpus truth
.claude/agent-memory/

# the compose volume of docker/compose.yml (spec 033 B-1)
docker/.data/

# >>> statecraft managed ignores >>>
# Managed by Statecraft. Entries above and below this block are yours and are
# never reordered, rewritten or removed. Delete the whole block to opt out.
# spec-spine: transient metadata and runtime state
#
# spec-spine writes wall-clock metadata here. It is the one
# non-deterministic artifact and is excluded from every determinism and
# golden check, so it must never be committed.
.statecraft/derived/**/build-meta.json

# The declared state root (spec 036): a tool's own working files,
# ungoverned and outside every content hash.
.statecraft/state/

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .statecraft/derived/spec-registry/ and
# .statecraft/derived/codebase-index/ are the committed shard trees.
#
# Committing them is what makes `compile --check` and `index check` a
# freshness gate on a pull request: CI compares the corpus against what
# the branch committed. Not committing them means regenerating in CI
# before every gate step instead. Both are legitimate; the scaffold
# takes neither, because opting you out of the gate silently would be a
# decision made on your behalf. To choose the second, add:
#
#   .statecraft/derived/
# The repository-local spec-spine the setup profile installs.
.tooling/
# <<< statecraft managed ignores <<<
